What is 3D Additive Metal Powder?
3D Additive Metal Powder refers to fine metallic particles specifically designed for additive manufacturing (3D printing) processes. These powders are engineered to meet stringent requirements for metal alloys and are produced through advanced techniques such as gas atomization, plasma atomization, or mechanical alloying. They exhibit precise particle size distribution and high sphericity to ensure optimal flowability, layer adhesion, and sintering performance in powder bed fusion (PBF), binder jetting, and directed energy deposition (DED) systems.

These specialized materials enable the production of complex, high-performance components across critical industries. For instance, titanium powders dominate aerospace applications due to their exceptional strength-to-weight ratio, while cobalt-chrome alloys are preferred for medical implants requiring biocompatibility and durability. Recent material innovations, including high-entropy alloys and nano-structured powders, are further expanding application potential across industrial sectors.

